# Ownership for codeowners-tool itself.
#
# A CODEOWNERS tool whose own repository has no CODEOWNERS fails its own A-11
# check ("the CODEOWNERS file itself has no owner — anyone with write access can
# change ownership rules unreviewed"), which is a fair thing for a reviewer to
# notice before trusting the tool's judgement about anyone else's repo.
#
# One rule, deliberately. This repository has a single maintainer, so narrower
# rules would name the same owner and buy nothing — and every rule that matches
# no tracked file is an A-4 finding, while every rule fully covered by a later
# one is an A-6 finding. `*` matches every path including this file, which is
# what A-11 asks for. Add narrower rules when there is a second owner to name.
#
# Verify with the tool itself:
#     codeowners-tool audit
